^page{G1North}{^T{Gauge One North}}{^eventsPrimary}{^g1NorthSecondary}{

^cbox{^tbox{^h1{Gauge 1 North}

^PAR{The first Gauge 1 North show was organised by the Yorkshire Group in 2010 . The event has gone from strength to strength since then. 

The 2026 show is on ^bf{Saturday 11 July} from 10.00 to 16.00 at the Agricultural Business Centre in Bakewell, Derbyshire, ^postcode{DE45}{1AH}; entry is £8.

Gauge 1 North is open to the public, and offers particularly good support from the trade, with around 30 suppliers attending every year.

        ^cbox{
           ^PAR{^link{Bakewell}{https://www.bakewell.co.uk} is a charming small town on the banks of the River Wye in the Derbyshire White Peaks. ^link{Chatsworth}{https://www.chatsworth.org} and ^link{Haddon Hall}{https://www.haddonhall.co.uk} are nearby, and it makes an ideal location for a weekend away. For more information about the area, see ^link{this site.}{https://visitpeakdistrict.com/}
}
           ^hgap
           ^image{BakewellPanorama.jpg}{Panoramic view of Bakewell: image credit - Peter McDermott under licence CC BY-SA 2.0}
           ^hgap	
        }


The Agricultural Business Centre is a compact venue, all on one level with extensive ^link{parking}{https://www.derbyshiredales.gov.uk/parking-roads-and-travel/parking/car-park-locations#h3} on site. Please make sure to follow any parking notices: the area to the front of the hall is reserved for coach drop off and blue badge holders. The centre of Bakewell is a ten minute walk from the hall.

Refreshments are available on site on Saturday at the ^link{Farmers' Feast}{https://farmersfeastbakewell.co.uk/} cafe next to the show hall. 
}

